Add the experimental, default-off `--consistent-obligation-checks` option to prepare and check matching implicit obligations once using the existing local assertion machinery.
Method and iterator postconditions are checked at each body exit while reveal scopes are active; nonchecking procedure copies retain their interface semantics.
Method/function preconditions and visible type/conversion/allocation obligations use a single prepared check. Explicit assertions, existing fuel rules and legacy hide/reveal scopes are preserved.

Certified contract preparation preserves guards while binding eligible private function arguments once; actual obligation checks, source state and fuel remain unchanged.

Opt-in method-call preparation constructs complete can-call support at the standard assertion point, after well-formedness preparation and before the existing single check, without an extra early construction.

Opt-in local postconditions use standard complete can-call construction after well-formedness preparation, while inherited and statement-expression clauses retain their original leading support and reveal effects.
